  "id": "Compound::DB00869 - Gene::23632",
  "verbalization": "Dorzolamide appears to interact with multiple calcium-binding proteins through a shared mechanism of participation in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. The evidence suggests that Dorzolamide binds to Ca5a, Ca12, or Ca6, all of which participate in the same biochemical process. This indicates that Dorzolamide may influence the activity of these calcium-binding proteins, potentially through a common pathway. The presence of multiple binding sites on different calcium proteins, all leading to the same downstream effect, supports the idea that Dorzolamide modulates calcium-related processes by targeting a shared functional component. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Dorzolamide in regulating calcium homeostasis, though the exact mechanism of interaction with Ca14 remains to be fully elucidated.",
